## Three.xtl -- the facade of the three extension: interactive 3D in a
## browser. A scene is the calls of a player -- the text Cycles.xtl's
## functions write (cy:s_tage, cy:f_acade, cy:b_oxes, cy:f_leet, cy:f_ly
## and the rest) without cy:head, Blender's player. Here the player is
## written with Three.js and draws the same calls in real time: ride
## the camera's flight, fly or walk. th:s_how! draws a scene in the
## page the program runs in (X_eTaL as WebAssembly); th:p_age! writes a
## directory to serve, from the command line.
## Import: "th:" u_se< "Three"
## Run with xetal-x (xetal-x --ext DIR puts this directory on XETAL_PATH).
## Each signature line is written out by the binding macro (lib/Ffi.xtlm).

"ffi:" u_se< "Ffi"

## th:a_bout @: the extension's name and version.
"a_bout : unit -> text"          ffi:b_ind< "three/about"
## th:s_how! scene: draws the scene in the page, in place of the one
## shown before; how many calls it holds. From the command line there
## is no page and nothing is drawn (the count is still given).
"s_how! : text -> int"           ffi:b_ind< "three/show"
## dir th:p_age! scene: writes a directory to serve (under the working
## directory, or XETAL_THREE_ROOT) -- index.html, the player, Three.js
## and the scene's calls -- made whole each time; how many files.
"p_age! : text text -> int"      ffi:b_ind< "three/page"

## The native package behind these functions.
l:package := "three"
